fix: review round 5 — fact contradictions, verify-engine gate wired into Quick Start, systemd unit, robustness

documentation truthfulness:
- storage-management: claim that a model update with a raised context window
  "automatically benefits" is wrong -- max_model_len lives in the cache
  namespace, so a context change=&gt;new namespace=&gt;old cache NOT reused. Corrected
  in EN/RU/ZH + wiki Storage-and-Eviction trio.
- eviction math: 0.9 trigger x 0.9 of used after one cycle = ~0.81 of budget,
  not the previously-stated 0.85. Fixed in EN/RU/ZH + wiki trio.
- dedup/references wording: LMCache keys map 1:1 to chunk objects; there is no
  caller-side refcount -- wording clamped to match this in EN.
- final-report bytes-per-token formula: NVMe stores the FULL KV tensor not
  per-rank; removed "/ tp_size" from the delivered total-bytes-per-token line.
- verify-engine-identity.sh --duplicated as a step-8 gate in Quick Start EN/RU/ZH
  (it was previously only documented in final-report); explains INCONCLUSIVE
  semantics ("unverifiable value = refused cache reuse, never a silent PASS").

localization / banners:
- every docs/*.md banner now matches its own locale (EN=Language versions,
  RU=Языковые версии, ZH=本页其他语言版本); Russian banners in English files are gone.

new scripts:
- scripts/print-recipe-image.sh -- robust IMAGE-digest extraction from any recipe
  tp4.env.example (handles commented template lines, validates @sha256:<64hex&gt;),
  replaces the fragile grep|sed one-liner in Quick Start EN/RU/ZH.

new systemd/lmcache-server.service -- proper unit for systemd hosts
(reboot-surviving, journald logs, restart-on-failure) vs \"setsid nohup\" convenience
mode.

preflight extended per review:
- python3.12 / python3-venv presence check (Debian 12 default is 3.11).
- free-space-vs-budget check on the cache filesystem.
- cache-root permission 0700 check.
- loopback-only listener check on lmcache request + HTTP ports.

license:
- LICENSE is now the official Apache-2.0 text; NOTICE carries required
  attribution credit (author sikkatu / repo URL) that Section 4(d) obliges
  users and forks to reproduce.